  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses exclusively on the minimum probability of each lottery and selects the one with the higher value. The individual in the verbal report does not mention or focus on the minimum probability per se; instead, they compare the difference in probabilities (1 percentage point) in relation to the difference in payoffs (100 Euros). This suggests a trade-off reasoning rather than a decision based solely on maximizing the minimum probability. Although the individual references probabilities, they do so in a comparative, incremental way (1% difference) rather than identifying or using the 'minimum probability' as a decision rule. There is no indication that the individual identified 34% and 33% as 'minimum probabilities' of the lotteries or used them categorically. Therefore, the structure of the reasoning in the report does not align with the decision reason. The individual seems to weigh probability and outcome together, not apply a minimum-probability-maximizing rule.",
